169: # Game Spec: Tribe Out / Bộ Lạc Out
170: 
171: *Full implementation prompt for the coding agent.*
172: 
173: ## Overview
174: 
175: Grid-based escape puzzle similar to Animal Out / Traffic Escape, themed as a tribe camp puzzle. Player taps characters to make them escape in their fixed facing direction.
176: 
177: ## Core Rules
178: 
179: - Board is a 2D grid (5×5, 6×6, or 7×7).
180: - Each movable character has a fixed direction: `up | down | left | right`.
181: - Tap a unit → check path in its direction until board edge.
182:   - **Clear path:** unit escapes, removed from board. No life lost.
183:   - **Blocked path:** bump animation, subtract 1 life.
184: - Level won when all required movable units escape.
185: - Level lost when lives reach 0 (default: 3 lives).
186: - Escaped units no longer block cells.
187: 
188: ## Required UI
189: 
190: **Top bar:** Lives (hearts) | Level number | Escaped progress (e.g. "4/12")
191: 
192: **Board:** Centered, responsive, playable at 375px mobile width.
193: 
194: **Bottom controls:** Restart | Hint (placeholder/disabled) | Next Level (post-win only)
195: 
196: **Win overlay:** "Level Complete" | escaped count | coins earned | Next Level + Replay buttons
197: 
198: **Lose overlay:** "Out of lives" | Restart button
199: 
200: ## Scoring & Persistence
201: - Each escaped unit: +10 coins
202: - Level complete bonus: +50 coins
203: - Remaining lives bonus: `livesRemaining × 20`
204: - Store `totalCoins` and `highestUnlockedLevel` in localStorage. No backend.
205: 
206: ## Data Types
207: 
208: ```ts
209: type Direction = "up" | "down" | "left" | "right";
210: 
211: type BoardEntity = {
212:   id: string;
213:   type: "unit" | "obstacle";
214:   assetKey: string;
215:   row: number;
216:   col: number;
217:   width: number;
218:   height: number;
219:   direction?: Direction;
220:   escaped?: boolean;
221: };
222: 
223: type TribeOutLevel = {
224:   id: number;
225:   boardRows: number;
226:   boardCols: number;
227:   lives: number;
228:   tutorialText?: string;
229:   entities: BoardEntity[];
230: };
231: ```
232: 
233: ## Required Pure Functions
234: 
235: 1. `getOccupiedCells(entity)` — all cells occupied, supports width/height
236: 2. `isInsideBoard(row, col, boardRows, boardCols)`
237: 3. `buildOccupancyMap(entities)` — maps cell → entity id, ignores escaped units
238: 4. `getForwardCellsUntilExit(unit, level)` — full front edge in direction until board edge
239: 5. `canExit(unit, level)` — true if all forward cells empty
240: 6. `applyTapUnit(unitId, state)` — core state transition
241: 7. `resetLevel(levelId)` — reloads original level
242: 8. `goToNextLevel()` — loads next level
243: 
244: ## File Structure
245: 
246: ```
247: src/features/tribe-out/types.ts
248: src/features/tribe-out/levels.ts
249: src/features/tribe-out/gameLogic.ts
250: src/features/tribe-out/TribeOutGame.tsx
251: src/features/tribe-out/TribeOutBoard.tsx
252: src/features/tribe-out/TribeOutEntity.tsx
253: src/features/tribe-out/TribeOutHUD.tsx
254: src/features/tribe-out/TribeOutOverlay.tsx
255: src/features/tribe-out/tribeOut.css
256: ```
257: 
258: ## Level Progression (10 levels minimum)
259: 
260: | Level | Grid | Units | Notes |
261: |-------|------|-------|-------|
262: | 1 | 5×5 | 3 | No obstacles. Teach tap-to-exit. |
263: | 2 | 5×5 | 4 | One unit blocks another. |
264: | 3 | 5×5 | 4 | Add one obstacle. |
265: | 4 | 6×6 | 5 | Multiple directions. |
266: | 5 | 6×6 | 5 | Add 2×1 unit. |
267: | 6 | 6×6 | 6 | More blockers. |
268: | 7 | 6×6 | 6 | Requires correct order. |
269: | 8 | 6×6 | 7 | Obstacles create narrow exits. |
270: | 9 | 7×7 | 8 | More units, still readable. |
271: | 10 | 7×7 | 9 | Mixed 1×1 and 2×1, order required. |
272: 
273: ## Direction Indicators
274: 
275: Every movable unit must show its direction. Minimum acceptable: arrow symbol on unit (↑ ↓ ← →), visible on mobile.
276: 
277: ## Animation (CSS-based)
278: 1. **Idle:** subtle breathing/bounce
279: 2. **Escape:** slide in direction + fade out
280: 3. **Bump:** slight forward then back + shake
281: 4. **Win/Lose overlays:** pop animation
282: 
283: Prioritize correct game state over visual polish.
284: 
285: ## Responsive Requirements
286: - Desktop: board centered, max ~640px wide
287: - Mobile: `min(92vw, available-height-based-size)`, no horizontal scroll
288: - Test at: 375×667, 390×844, 430×932, 768×1024, 1440×900
289: 
290: ## Acceptance Criteria
291: 1. Game opens without runtime errors
292: 2. Level 1 immediately playable
293: 3. Clear unit tap → exit animation + escaped count update
294: 4. Blocked unit tap → bump + life subtracted
295: 5. Escaped units no longer block board
296: 6. Hearts/lives update correctly
297: 7. Win overlay on all units escaped
298: 8. Lose overlay on lives = 0
299: 9. Restart resets level fully
300: 10. Next level loads correctly
301: 11. At least 10 levels exist
302: 12. Mobile viewport playable, no horizontal overflow
303: 13. Follows this DESIGN.md
304: 14. No backend, leaderboard, auth, shop, or PixiJS at v1
305: 
306: ## Implementation Order
307: - **Phase 1:** Types → levels → pure game logic → simple board rendering → playable loop
308: - **Phase 2:** HUD + overlays + localStorage
309: - **Phase 3:** DESIGN.md styling + CSS animations
310: - **Phase 4:** Responsive testing + fixes
</file>

