 69: ## Confirmed defects and design debt
 70: 
 71: ### Interaction boundary defect
 72: 
 73: `TribeOutEntity.tsx` currently treats switches as interactive because `isInteractive` excludes only obstacle and gate. A switch receives `role="button"`, tab focus, click, and keyboard activation.
 74: 
 75: `applyTapUnit` rejects only obstacles and escaped entities before `canExit`. A switch can reach the blocked-tap path and lose a life.
 76: 
 77: `applyRotateUnit` always decrements a charge after mapping, even when `unitId` does not name a live unit. A non-unit or missing target can consume a charge.
 78: 
 79: ### Economy without gameplay purpose
 80: 
 81: Coins are present in:
 82: 
 83: - `GameState` and `TribeOutProgressSnapshot`;
 84: - `gameLogic.ts` reward math;
 85: - `tribeOutStorage.ts`;
 86: - `TribeOutGame.tsx` hints and persistence;
 87: - `TribeOutHUD.tsx`;
 88: - `TribeOutOverlay.tsx`;
 89: - `screens/Dashboard.tsx`;
 90: - tests, CSS, and the viewport audit.
 91: 
 92: The economy is being removed by this specification.
 93: 
 94: ### Hint lifecycle defect
 95: 
 96: `TribeOutGame.tsx` creates the hint-clear timeout without retaining or clearing it on unmount, restart, or level transition. The new runtime contract must own this timer in a ref and clear it.
 97: 
 98: ### Solver incompleteness
 99: 
100: `scripts/solver.ts`:
101: 
102: - checks only level 22;
103: - performs greedy exits only;
104: - does not model rotate, switch, gate, validation, budgets, reports, or replay verification.
105: 
106: ### Generator shallowness
107: 
108: `scripts/gen_levels.cjs`:
109: 
110: - places obstacles first;
111: - accepts only units whose own path is initially clear;
112: - probabilistically makes later units block earlier units;
113: - uses one broad algorithm for most of the catalog;
114: - does not generate gates/switches after the handcrafted tutorial;
115: - does not guarantee phase-specific difficulty targets.
116: 
117: ### Invalid authored data
