20: ```
21: 
22: The second validate/solve/report sequence verifies the generated committed catalog rather than only in-memory candidates.
23: 
24: ## Clean-checkout verification
25: 
26: Before final acceptance, create a clean verification environment from the final commit or use a clean worktree. Run:
27: 
28: ```bash
29: npm ci
30: npm run typecheck
31: npm test
32: npm run build
33: npm run levels:validate
34: npm run levels:solve
35: npm run levels:report
36: ```
37: 
38: `levels:generate` must also work from clean checkout, but it may produce deterministic files whose diff must be empty against committed generated output.
39: 
40: Required check:
41: 
42: ```bash
43: npm run levels:generate
44: git diff --exit-code -- src/features/tribe-out/levels.ts reports/levels
45: ```
46: 
47: Adjust report paths if timestamp fields are intentionally excluded from committed deterministic reports. Committed outputs must not contain nondeterministic timestamps that create false diffs; runtime metadata timestamps may be written to non-committed execution evidence instead.
48: 
49: ## Hard release gates
50: 
51: - zero TypeScript errors in app and tools;
52: - zero failing tests;
53: - successful Vite build;
54: - exactly 100 valid levels;
55: - exactly 100 solvable levels;
56: - zero `INCONCLUSIVE` release levels;
57: - every solver trace replays to win;
58: - every level has a manifest;
59: - every level has a difficulty report;
60: - every out-of-band metric has an explicit approved exception;
61: - no unused mechanic entity in generated levels;
62: - no economy runtime, persistence, UI, test, CSS, or documentation behavior;
63: - stable level IDs and migration tests pass;
64: - viewport audit passes;
65: - representative manual QA passes;
66: - initial triage findings are fully resolved;
67: - no unrelated worktree changes are overwritten.
68: 
69: ## Determinism gates
70: 
71: - same seed + generator version + specification version produces byte-identical normalized level data;
72: - solver action order and trace are stable;
73: - analyzer sample seeds are stable;
74: - report level ordering is stable;
75: - generated `levels.ts` is stable;
76: - repeated progress migration is idempotent.
77: 
78: ## Performance gates
79: 
80: - 40-independent-unit fixture passes the linear fast path.
81: - Every release level solves inside declared state/time budgets.
82: - Full catalog validate + solve + report completes within a documented CI budget.
83: - Browser remains responsive on representative phase-5 level at supported mobile viewport.
84: 
85: ## Documentation gates
86: 
87: Update stale current-state documents that claim:
88: 
89: - only 10 levels;
90: - active coin economy;
91: - no PixiJS at all;
92: - obsolete runtime structure.
93: 
94: Do not rewrite historical audit records unless they claim to be current. Prefer marking historical documents as superseded with a link to current architecture.
</file>

<file path="doc/goal/quality/03_MANUAL_QA.md">
 1: # Manual QA Protocol
 2: 
 3: Record date, commit, browser, viewport, level ID, steps, and result.
 4: 
 5: ## Phase representatives
 6: 
 7: Test at least:
 8: 
 9: - Phase 1: first exit lesson, blocked-tap lesson, multi-cell lesson, rotate lesson, gate lesson.
10: - Phase 2: chain, fork/join, multi-cell structural blocker.
11: - Phase 3: gate branch, short gate chain, required rotate-to-switch.
12: - Phase 4: competing rotate choices and intentional dead end.
13: - Phase 5: deepest causal level, largest board, two-rotate level.
14: 
15: ## Required checks
16: 
17: ### Interaction
18: 
19: - only units focus and activate;
20: - switch/gate/obstacle clicks and keyboard actions do nothing;
21: - invalid rotate targets do not consume charge;
22: - blocked unit bumps and loses exactly one life.
23: 
24: ### State
25: 
26: - successful exit opens crossed switch target gate;
27: - gate stays open;
28: - restart fully resets gate, switch, units, timer, lives, hints, and rotate charges;
29: - next level loads correct stable ID;
30: - Dashboard and Settings preserve progress;
31: - level 100 completion does not corrupt unlock state.
32: 
33: ### Economy removal
34: 
35: - no coin value in HUD;
36: - no hint price;
37: - no coin reward on exit/win;
38: - no coin badge in win overlay;
39: - no coin section in Dashboard;
40: - old coin localStorage value has no effect.
41: 
42: ### Persistence
43: 
44: - legacy save migrates without crash;
45: - valid unlock/current position is preserved;
46: - old stars reset once for the redesigned catalog;
47: - new stars survive reload;
48: - clear progress resets to level 1;
49: - private/incognito or blocked storage still allows play.
50: 
51: ### Responsive and readability
52: 
53: At each required viewport:
54: 
55: - no page scroll;
56: - HUD and controls visible;
57: - board not clipped beyond usability;
58: - arrows readable;
59: - gates and switches visually distinguishable;
60: - multi-cell footprints understandable;
61: - phase-5 choices do not require pixel guessing.
62: 
63: ### Lifecycle
64: 
65: In React Strict Mode development:
66: 
67: - no duplicate Pixi canvas;
68: - no duplicate audio listeners;
69: - no warning about state update after unmount;
70: - restart/next during active hint or bump timer causes no stale update;
71: - background boom timer cleans up.
72: 
73: ### Reduced motion
74: 
75: With reduced motion enabled:
76: 
77: - puzzle state remains understandable;
78: - escape/bump state is not hidden;
79: - no perpetual breathing animation is required to identify interaction;
80: - overlays and controls remain usable.
