<file path="doc/goal/quality/04_EVIDENCE_AND_COMPLETION_PROTOCOL.md">
  1: # Evidence and Completion Protocol
  2: 
  3: ## Baseline evidence
  4: 
  5: Before changes, capture:
  6: 
  7: ```bash
  8: pwd
  9: git branch --show-current
 10: git rev-parse HEAD
 11: git status --short
 12: git diff --stat
 13: git diff
 14: ```
 15: 
 16: Store a copy under:
 17: 
 18: ```text
 19: reports/goal-execution/baseline/
 20: ```
 21: 
 22: When the worktree is dirty, record every out-of-scope entry and do not claim it was created by this assignment.
 23: 
 24: ## Per-gate evidence
 25: 
 26: For each gate in `IMPLEMENTATION_ORDER.md`, record:
 27: 
 28: - files changed;
 29: - diff stat;
 30: - relevant raw diff;
 31: - commands run;
 32: - raw test/tool output;
 33: - acceptance criteria result;
 34: - unresolved risk;
 35: - next gate decision.
 36: 
 37: Use:
 38: 
 39: ```text
 40: reports/goal-execution/gate-00.md
 41: ...
 42: reports/goal-execution/gate-12.md
 43: ```
 44: 
 45: ## Generated reports
 46: 
 47: Required:
 48: 
 49: ```text
 50: reports/levels/validation.json
 51: reports/levels/solutions.json
 52: reports/levels/solutions.md
 53: reports/levels/difficulty.json
 54: reports/levels/difficulty.csv
 55: reports/levels/difficulty.md
 56: reports/goal-execution/triage-initial.txt
 57: reports/goal-execution/triage-resolution.md
 58: reports/goal-execution/manual-qa.md
 59: reports/goal-execution/final-verification.txt
 60: ```
 61: 
 62: ## Final git evidence
 63: 
 64: Capture:
 65: 
 66: ```bash
 67: git status --short
 68: git diff --stat
 69: git diff --name-status
 70: git diff
 71: ```
 72: 
 73: If changes are committed during the repository workflow, also provide:
 74: 
 75: ```bash
 76: git log --oneline --decorate -n 20
 77: ```
 78: 
 79: The final report must distinguish assignment changes from baseline unrelated changes.
 80: 
 81: ## Raw command evidence
 82: 
 83: Never summarize a command as passed without preserving its raw stdout/stderr and exit code.
 84: 
 85: ## Final completion report
 86: 
 87: Return these exact sections:
 88: 
 89: ```text
 90: STATUS
 91: REPOSITORY
 92: BRANCH_AND_COMMITS
 93: BASELINE_WORKTREE
 94: TRIAGE_ANALYSIS_AND_RESOLUTION
 95: ARCHITECTURE_IMPLEMENTED
 96: ECONOMY_REMOVAL
 97: PROGRESS_MIGRATION
 98: LEVEL_CATALOG_SUMMARY
 99: VALIDATOR_SUMMARY
100: SOLVER_SUMMARY
101: DIFFICULTY_SUMMARY
102: FILES_CREATED_MODIFIED_DELETED
103: COMMANDS_AND_RAW_RESULTS
104: MANUAL_QA
105: OUT_OF_SCOPE_WORKTREE_ENTRIES
106: KNOWN_LIMITATIONS
107: DEFINITION_OF_DONE_CHECKLIST
108: ```
109: 
110: `STATUS` must be exactly one of:
111: 
112: ```text
113: GOAL_ACCEPTED
114: GOAL_BLOCKED
115: GOAL_FAILED
116: ```
117: 
118: ## `GOAL_BLOCKED`
119: 
120: Use only when an external capability, missing source, unrecoverable repository state, or impossible specification conflict prevents completion.
121: 
122: Include:
123: 
124: - exact blocker;
125: - evidence;
126: - affected requirements;
127: - work completed safely;
128: - changes that must not be treated as accepted.
129: 
130: ## `GOAL_FAILED`
131: 
132: Use when implementation was attempted but repository correctness or verification is broken and no safe completion was achieved.
133: 
134: ## No partial success
135: 
136: Do not use `GOAL_ACCEPTED` when:
137: 
138: - any release level is invalid, unsolvable, or inconclusive;
139: - tests/build/typecheck fail;
140: - economy remains reachable;
141: - progress migration is unverified;
142: - generated output is nondeterministic;
143: - initial triage findings remain unresolved;
144: - manual evidence is missing;
145: - source claims contradict raw evidence.
</file>

