 1: # Approved Overrides and Decisions
 2: 
 3: This file records decisions made after the strategic plan was written. These decisions are authoritative.
 4: 
 5: ## Repository
 6: 
 7: ```text
 8: /home/pro/Downloads/intern/11_Escape
 9: ```
10: 
11: The final ZIP is intended to be extracted into:
12: 
13: ```text
14: /home/pro/Downloads/intern/11_Escape/goal
15: ```
16: 
17: ## Full catalog
18: 
19: The assignment covers exactly 100 released levels:
20: 
21: | Phase | Levels | Primary character |
22: | --- | --- | --- |
23: | Phase 1 | `level-001`–`level-020` | Foundation and explicit teaching |
24: | Phase 2 | `level-021`–`level-040` | Structured monotonic dependency |
25: | Phase 3 | `level-041`–`level-060` | Stateful gate/switch reasoning |
26: | Phase 4 | `level-061`–`level-080` | Strategic combination and rotate resource decisions |
27: | Phase 5 | `level-081`–`level-100` | Expert causal planning |
28: 
29: Each phase uses its own catalog construction algorithm and target bands. A single generic random-placement algorithm is forbidden.
30: 
31: ## Level identity
32: 
33: Every level uses one stable string identifier:
34: 
35: ```text
36: level-001
37: level-002
38: ...
39: level-100
40: ```
41: 
42: Do not append `v2`, content hashes, or content-version suffixes to level IDs. Catalog-wide changes use `levelSetVersion`.
43: 
44: ## Economy removal
45: 
46: Remove the economy completely. This includes:
47: 
48: - `coins` state and persistence;
49: - per-unit rewards;
50: - win/completion rewards;
51: - first-clear rewards;
52: - reward claim records;
53: - replay anti-farming logic;
54: - hint costs and insufficient-coin behavior;
55: - coin HUD and Dashboard content;
56: - coin overlay content;
57: - economy-specific CSS, tests, constants, imports, and documentation.
58: 
59: Hints remain free. `hintsUsed` remains because the star calculation uses it.
60: 
61: ## Progress retained
62: 
63: Retain:
64: 
65: - stable level IDs;
66: - unlocked level IDs;
67: - current level ID;
68: - best stars by level ID;
69: - progress schema version;
70: - level-set version.
71: 
72: For the first release of the redesigned 100-level catalog, reset stars for all 100 levels exactly once because every level is in redesign scope. Preserve valid unlock progression and current position.
73: 
74: ## Figma triage
75: 
76: The implementing agent must:
77: 
78: 1. Read the installed `figma-triage` skill instructions.
79: 2. Run its analyze operation before puzzle-system implementation.
80: 3. Save the complete raw analysis.
81: 4. Classify and remove every confirmed redundant item in that analysis.
82: 5. Validate the cleanup with the repository's actual build, typecheck, and tests.
83: 6. Freeze the triage scope.
84: 7. Never invoke the skill again during this assignment.
85: 
86: A finding may be retained only when proven to be a false positive with source evidence. The evidence must be listed in the initial triage report.
87: 
88: ## Specification authority
89: 
90: The implementing model must follow the specification completely. When source conflicts with the specification, the model may remove or rewrite the source. It must not preserve contradictory legacy behavior.
