  152: 
  153: # 11_Escape Codex workflow
  154: 
  155: Use this skill for any Codex task in this repo.
  156: 
  157: ## Scope
  158: 
  159: - Applies to `11_Escape` only.
  160: - Use the repo workflow file at `../../../workflow.md` as the source of truth.
  161: - This skill is tailored for Codex-owned changes.
  162: 
  163: ## Branch policy
  164: 
  165: - Work on `codex` for Codex-owned changes.
  166: - Never mix Codex work into `agy`.
  167: - Use `dev` only for verified merge aggregation.
  168: - Merge to `main` only after `dev` is stable.
  169: 
  170: ## When you start
  171: 
  172: 1. Check `git status`.
  173: 2. Confirm the current branch.
  174: 3. Identify whether the task is Codex-owned.
  175: 4. Read `../../../workflow.md` if needed for the exact merge flow.
  176: 
  177: ## Execution rules
  178: 
  179: - Keep each change scoped to one purpose.
  180: - Prefer small, reviewable commits.
  181: - Do not disturb unrelated dirty worktree files.
  182: - If a change belongs to another agent, stop and hand it off conceptually instead of blending branches.
  183: 
  184: ## Required order
  185: 
  186: 1. Create or switch to `codex`.
  187: 2. Make the change.
  188: 3. Commit on `codex`.
  189: 4. Push `codex`.
  190: 5. Merge into `dev`.
  191: 6. Test on `dev`.
  192: 7. Merge `dev` into `main` only when stable.
  193: 
  194: ## Files to update when needed
  195: 
  196: - `workflow.md` for shared process changes.
  197: - `CODEX_RULES.md` only if the repo keeps a separate Codex rule file and the change is Codex-specific.
