  212: # 11_Escape Gemini workflow
  213: 
  214: Use this skill for any Gemini/AGY task in this repo.
  215: 
  216: ## Scope
  217: 
  218: - Applies to `11_Escape` only.
  219: - Use the repo workflow file at `../../../workflow.md` as the source of truth.
  220: - This skill is tailored for Gemini/AGY-owned changes.
  221: 
  222: ## Branch policy
  223: 
  224: - Work on `agy` for Gemini/AGY-owned changes.
  225: - Never mix AGY work into `codex`.
  226: - Use `dev` only for verified merge aggregation.
  227: - Merge to `main` only after `dev` is stable.
  228: 
  229: ## When you start
  230: 
  231: 1. Check `git status`.
  232: 2. Confirm the current branch.
  233: 3. Identify whether the task is AGY-owned.
  234: 4. Read `../../../workflow.md` if needed for the exact merge flow.
  235: 
  236: ## Execution rules
  237: 
  238: - Keep each change scoped to one purpose.
  239: - Prefer small, reviewable commits.
  240: - Do not disturb unrelated dirty worktree files.
  241: - If a change belongs to Codex, stop and hand it off conceptually instead of blending branches.
  242: 
  243: ## Required order
  244: 
  245: 1. Create or switch to `agy`.
  246: 2. Make the change.
  247: 3. Commit on `agy`.
  248: 4. Push `agy`.
  249: 5. Merge into `dev`.
  250: 6. Test on `dev`.
  251: 7. Merge `dev` into `main` only when stable.
  252: 
  253: ## Files to update when needed
  254: 
  255: - `workflow.md` for shared process changes.
  256: - `AGY.md` or `.gemini`-local rule files only if the repo keeps a separate AGY rule file and the change is AGY-specific.
