  623: # Game Spec: Tribe Out / Bộ Lạc Out
  624: 
  625: *Full implementation prompt for the coding agent.*
  626: 
  627: ## Overview
  628: 
  629: Grid-based escape puzzle similar to Animal Out / Traffic Escape, themed as a tribe camp puzzle. Player taps characters to make them escape in their fixed facing direction.
  630: 
  631: ## Core Rules
  632: 
  633: - Board is a 2D grid (5×5, 6×6, or 7×7).
  634: - Each movable character has a fixed direction: `up | down | left | right`.
  635: - Tap a unit → check path in its direction until board edge.
  636:   - **Clear path:** unit escapes, removed from board. No life lost.
  637:   - **Blocked path:** bump animation, subtract 1 life.
  638: - Level won when all required movable units escape.
  639: - Level lost when lives reach 0 (default: 3 lives).
  640: - Escaped units no longer block cells.
  641: 
  642: ## Required UI
  643: 
  644: **Top bar:** Lives (hearts) | Level number | Escaped progress (e.g. "4/12")
  645: 
  646: **Board:** Centered, responsive, playable at 375px mobile width.
  647: 
  648: **Bottom controls:** Restart | Hint (placeholder/disabled) | Next Level (post-win only)
  649: 
  650: **Win overlay:** "Level Complete" | escaped count | coins earned | Next Level + Replay buttons
  651: 
  652: **Lose overlay:** "Out of lives" | Restart button
  653: 
  654: ## Scoring & Persistence
  655: - Each escaped unit: +10 coins
  656: - Level complete bonus: +50 coins
  657: - Remaining lives bonus: `livesRemaining × 20`
  658: - Store `totalCoins` and `highestUnlockedLevel` in localStorage. No backend.
  659: 
  660: ## Data Types
  661: 
  662: ```ts
  663: type Direction = "up" | "down" | "left" | "right";
  664: 
  665: type BoardEntity = {
  666:   id: string;
  667:   type: "unit" | "obstacle";
  668:   assetKey: string;
  669:   row: number;
  670:   col: number;
  671:   width: number;
  672:   height: number;
  673:   direction?: Direction;
  674:   escaped?: boolean;
  675: };
  676: 
  677: type TribeOutLevel = {
  678:   id: number;
  679:   boardRows: number;
  680:   boardCols: number;
  681:   lives: number;
  682:   tutorialText?: string;
  683:   entities: BoardEntity[];
  684: };
  685: ```
  686: 
  687: ## Required Pure Functions
  688: 
  689: 1. `getOccupiedCells(entity)` — all cells occupied, supports width/height
  690: 2. `isInsideBoard(row, col, boardRows, boardCols)`
  691: 3. `buildOccupancyMap(entities)` — maps cell → entity id, ignores escaped units
  692: 4. `getForwardCellsUntilExit(unit, level)` — full front edge in direction until board edge
  693: 5. `canExit(unit, level)` — true if all forward cells empty
  694: 6. `applyTapUnit(unitId, state)` — core state transition
  695: 7. `resetLevel(levelId)` — reloads original level
  696: 8. `goToNextLevel()` — loads next level
  697: 
  698: ## File Structure
  699: 
  700: ```
  701: src/features/tribe-out/types.ts
  702: src/features/tribe-out/levels.ts
  703: src/features/tribe-out/gameLogic.ts
  704: src/features/tribe-out/TribeOutGame.tsx
  705: src/features/tribe-out/TribeOutBoard.tsx
  706: src/features/tribe-out/TribeOutEntity.tsx
  707: src/features/tribe-out/TribeOutHUD.tsx
  708: src/features/tribe-out/TribeOutOverlay.tsx
  709: src/features/tribe-out/tribeOut.css
  710: ```
  711: 
  712: ## Level Progression (10 levels minimum)
  713: 
  714: | Level | Grid | Units | Notes |
  715: |-------|------|-------|-------|
  716: | 1 | 5×5 | 3 | No obstacles. Teach tap-to-exit. |
  717: | 2 | 5×5 | 4 | One unit blocks another. |
  718: | 3 | 5×5 | 4 | Add one obstacle. |
  719: | 4 | 6×6 | 5 | Multiple directions. |
  720: | 5 | 6×6 | 5 | Add 2×1 unit. |
  721: | 6 | 6×6 | 6 | More blockers. |
  722: | 7 | 6×6 | 6 | Requires correct order. |
  723: | 8 | 6×6 | 7 | Obstacles create narrow exits. |
  724: | 9 | 7×7 | 8 | More units, still readable. |
  725: | 10 | 7×7 | 9 | Mixed 1×1 and 2×1, order required. |
  726: 
  727: ## Direction Indicators
  728: 
  729: Every movable unit must show its direction. Minimum acceptable: arrow symbol on unit (↑ ↓ ← →), visible on mobile.
  730: 
  731: ## Animation (CSS-based)
  732: 1. **Idle:** subtle breathing/bounce
  733: 2. **Escape:** slide in direction + fade out
  734: 3. **Bump:** slight forward then back + shake
  735: 4. **Win/Lose overlays:** pop animation
  736: 
  737: Prioritize correct game state over visual polish.
  738: 
  739: ## Responsive Requirements
  740: - Desktop: board centered, max ~640px wide
  741: - Mobile: `min(92vw, available-height-based-size)`, no horizontal scroll
  742: - Test at: 375×667, 390×844, 430×932, 768×1024, 1440×900
  743: 
  744: ## Acceptance Criteria
  745: 1. Game opens without runtime errors
  746: 2. Level 1 immediately playable
  747: 3. Clear unit tap → exit animation + escaped count update
  748: 4. Blocked unit tap → bump + life subtracted
  749: 5. Escaped units no longer block board
  750: 6. Hearts/lives update correctly
  751: 7. Win overlay on all units escaped
  752: 8. Lose overlay on lives = 0
  753: 9. Restart resets level fully
  754: 10. Next level loads correctly
  755: 11. At least 10 levels exist
  756: 12. Mobile viewport playable, no horizontal overflow
  757: 13. Follows this DESIGN.md
  758: 14. No backend, leaderboard, auth, shop, or PixiJS at v1
  759: 
  760: ## Implementation Order
  761: - **Phase 1:** Types → levels → pure game logic → simple board rendering → playable loop
  762: - **Phase 2:** HUD + overlays + localStorage
  763: - **Phase 3:** DESIGN.md styling + CSS animations
  764: - **Phase 4:** Responsive testing + fixes
