38: - Tribe Out puzzle logic and types;
39: - Tribe Out runtime UI required by logic/economy removal;
40: - Tribe Out persistence;
41: - level data and level authoring tools;
42: - package scripts and TypeScript tool configuration;
43: - tests and fixtures;
44: - generated level reports;
45: - stale documentation that contradicts the released implementation;
46: - dead code/imports/files identified by the one-time triage analysis.
47: 
48: ## Protected scope
49: 
50: Do not redesign unrelated visual assets, audio architecture, background art, rendering style, or navigation. Preserve the current React/DOM entity rendering over a Pixi isometric backdrop. The whole game must not be migrated to Pixi.
51: 
52: Audio remains supported and must retain mute state, gesture unlock, visibility handling, external-buffer fallback, synthesized fallback, and disposal behavior.
53: 
54: ## Global invariants
55: 
56: - A live unit escapes only when its entire forward path is clear across its full leading edge.
57: - Blocked live-unit taps preserve the intended bump and life loss behavior.
58: - Invalid targets such as obstacle, gate, switch, missing entity, or escaped unit do not consume life or rotate charge.
59: - Multi-cell footprints work in all four directions.
60: - Closed gates block; open gates do not.
61: - Switches do not occupy blocking cells and activate only when crossed by a successful exit.
62: - Gate opening is one-way and permanent for the current attempt.
63: - Rotate is clockwise, level-configured, and charge-limited.
64: - All puzzle transitions are immutable and deterministic.
65: - All units escaped produces exactly one win transition.
66: - Lives reaching zero produces loss.
67: - Timer expiry does not itself lose the level; it affects stars only.
68: - Restart restores original puzzle state and configured charges.
69: - Progress is stable across Dashboard and Settings.
70: - Storage failure never crashes gameplay.
71: - The app remains a locked, non-scrolling single-screen experience.
72: - Pixi initialization and destruction remain safe under React Strict Mode.
73: - No duplicate timers, listeners, canvas instances, animations, or audio unlock handlers.
74: - No state update or Pixi mutation after unmount/destroy.
75: - Reduced-motion and accessibility behavior do not regress.
76: 
77: ## Completion statuses
78: 
79: The final report must use exactly one:
80: 
81: - `GOAL_ACCEPTED`
82: - `GOAL_BLOCKED`
83: - `GOAL_FAILED`
84: 
85: `GOAL_ACCEPTED` is allowed only when every Definition of Done item passes with raw evidence.
</file>

