  1: # 11_Escape Checkpoint
  2: 
  3: ## Purpose
  4: 
  5: This document captures what must stay clear before any future work continues on `11_Escape / Tribe Out`.
  6: 
  7: The project is no longer a raw Figma Make export. It is now a stabilized React DOM game with a locked single-screen shell, tested gameplay rules, shared game UI primitives, and cleaned production dependencies.
  8: 
  9: Use this file before adding assets, audio, animation, new levels, economy features, or any larger refactor.
 10: 
 11: ## 1. Layers
 12: 
 13: The codebase should keep these ownership layers separate.
 14: 
 15: ### App Layer
 16: 
 17: Files:
 18: 
 19: - `src/main.tsx`
 20: - `src/app/App.tsx`
 21: - `src/styles/globals.css`
 22: - `src/styles/index.css`
 23: 
 24: Purpose:
 25: 
 26: - Boot React.
 27: - Render the fixed single-screen viewport.
 28: - Own the countryside background.
 29: - Lock `html`, `body`, and `#root` so the page cannot scroll vertically or horizontally.
 30: - Keep the app at `100dvh` with safe-area padding handled inside the locked viewport.
 31: 
 32: Rules:
 33: 
 34: - Do not put gameplay rules here.
 35: - Do not add routing unless the game actually needs multiple screens.
 36: - Do not change the app into a landing page.
 37: - Do not let the page scroll to solve layout problems.
 38: 
 39: ### Shared Game UI Layer
 40: 
 41: Files:
 42: 
 43: - `src/components/game/GameShell.tsx`
 44: - `src/components/game/GameButton.tsx`
 45: - `src/components/game/HudStat.tsx`
 46: - `src/components/game/GameOverlayFrame.tsx`
 47: - `src/components/game/useMeasuredElementSize.ts`
 48: 
 49: Purpose:
 50: 
 51: - Provide generic game-screen structure.
 52: - Provide reusable button, HUD stat, overlay frame, and measured-area sizing patterns.
 53: - Keep the shell reusable for future small games without importing Tribe Out-specific logic.
 54: 
 55: Rules:
 56: 
 57: - Shared components must not import `src/features/tribe-out/*`.
 58: - Shared components should stay small and behavior-light.
 59: - Do not add abstractions here unless at least two places need the same structure.
 60: 
 61: ### Tribe Out Feature Layer
 62: 
 63: Files:
 64: 
 65: - `src/features/tribe-out/TribeOutGame.tsx`
 66: - `src/features/tribe-out/TribeOutBoard.tsx`
 67: - `src/features/tribe-out/TribeOutEntity.tsx`
 68: - `src/features/tribe-out/TribeOutHUD.tsx`
 69: - `src/features/tribe-out/TribeOutOverlay.tsx`
 70: - `src/features/tribe-out/AnimalSprite.tsx`
 71: - `src/features/tribe-out/tribeOut.css`
 72: 
 73: Purpose:
 74: 
 75: - Render the actual game.
 76: - Own Tribe Out-specific board, entity, HUD, overlay, and visual styling.
 77: - Connect shared shell components to game state.
 78: - Keep controls, board, HUD, and overlays visible inside one viewport.
 79: 
 80: Rules:
 81: 
 82: - Keep Tribe Out-specific UI here.
 83: - Keep board rendering as React DOM for v1.
 84: - Do not add PixiJS unless DOM performance becomes a real bottleneck.
 85: - Do not hide overflow in a way that makes board pieces or controls inaccessible.
 86: 
 87: ### Gameplay Logic Layer
 88: 
 89: Files:
 90: 
 91: - `src/features/tribe-out/gameLogic.ts`
 92: - `src/features/tribe-out/levels.ts`
 93: - `src/features/tribe-out/types.ts`
 94: - `src/features/tribe-out/gameLogic.test.ts`
 95: 
 96: Purpose:
 97: 
 98: - Own pure board rules.
 99: - Own level data.
100: - Own state transition behavior.
101: - Keep tests for core gameplay expectations.
102: 
103: Rules:
104: 
105: - `gameLogic.ts` should stay pure and testable.
106: - Do not call `localStorage`, browser APIs, audio, animation APIs, or DOM APIs inside pure logic.
107: - Every level must remain solvable.
108: - Every rule change should get a focused unit test.
109: 
110: ### Persistence Layer
111: 
112: Files:
113: 
114: - `src/features/tribe-out/tribeOutStorage.ts`
115: 
116: Purpose:
117: 
118: - Own browser storage for simple progress.
119: - Keep persistence outside pure gameplay logic.
120: 
121: Rules:
122: 
123: - Store only simple local progress in v1.
124: - No backend, auth, leaderboard, shop, ads, gacha, or online economy.
125: 
126: ## 2. Components
127: 
128: ### Current Shared Components
129: 
130: `GameShell`
131: 
132: - Provides the fixed game card structure.
133: - Contains header, optional notice, board area, and controls.
134: - The board area is the flexible region and is measured for sizing.
135: 
136: `GameButton`
137: 
138: - Provides reusable game button styling.
139: - Supports `primary` and `ghost` variants.
140: - Keeps a minimum usable target size.
141: 
142: `HudStat`
143: 
144: - Provides reusable HUD stat structure.
145: - Used for level, lives, escape progress, and coins.
146: 
147: `GameOverlayFrame`
148: 
149: - Provides reusable overlay card structure.
150: - Used by win and lose overlays.
151: 
152: `useMeasuredElementSize`
153: 
154: - Measures actual available space with `ResizeObserver`, `visualViewport`, and scheduled resize retries.
155: - Prevents board sizing from depending on guessed viewport constants.
156: 
157: ### Current Tribe Out Components
158: 
159: `TribeOutGame`
160: 
161: - Owns the active game state.
162: - Loads saved coins.
163: - Applies taps through pure logic.
164: - Persists win progress.
165: - Computes board cell size from the measured board area.
166: 
167: `TribeOutBoard`
168: 
169: - Renders the square grass grid and entity layer.
170: - Receives `cellSize` from the measured shell layout.
171: 
172: `TribeOutEntity`
173: 
174: - Renders units and obstacles.
175: - Handles click and keyboard activation.
176: - Owns entity escape and bump animations.
177: 
178: `TribeOutHUD`
179: 
180: - Displays lives, level, escaped count, and coins.
181: - Uses shared `HudStat`.
182: 
183: `TribeOutOverlay`
184: 
185: - Displays win and lose dialogs.
186: - Uses shared `GameOverlayFrame` and `GameButton`.
187: 
188: `AnimalSprite`
189: 
190: - Provides the current SVG fallback character visuals.
191: - Should remain available even if raster assets are added later.
192: 
193: ## 3. Levels
194: 
195: The current game has 10 levels in `src/features/tribe-out/levels.ts`.
196: 
197: Current level model:
198: 
199: - `id`
200: - `boardRows`
201: - `boardCols`
202: - `lives`
203: - optional `tutorialText`
204: - `entities`
205: 
206: Current entity model:
207: 
208: - `unit` or `obstacle`
209: - `row` and `col`
210: - `width` and `height`
211: - optional `direction`
212: - optional `escaped`
213: 
214: Current gameplay rules:
215: 
216: - Tapping a unit with a clear path makes it escape.
217: - Tapping a blocked unit costs one life.
218: - Escaped units no longer block other units.
219: - Obstacles always block.
220: - The level is won when every unit has escaped.
221: - The level is lost when lives reach zero.
222: - Restart resets the current level but keeps total coins.
223: - Next level loads the next level and keeps total coins.
224: 
225: Level safety requirements:
226: 
227: - Keep all 10 levels solvable.
228: - Preserve or update the solution comments when a level changes.
229: - Add tests for any new entity size or movement rule.
230: - Keep board sizes mobile-friendly.
231: - Do not add level mechanics that require scrolling.
232: 
233: ## 4. Current UI
234: 
235: Current UI state:
236: 
237: - The game is a single-screen countryside puzzle shell.
238: - The app viewport is fixed and non-scrolling.
239: - HUD is visible at the top.
240: - Board stays centered in the flexible board area.
241: - Controls stay visible at the bottom.
242: - Win and lose overlays fit inside the board area.
243: - Units support click, touch, and keyboard activation.
244: - Direction arrows remain visible on the units.
245: 
246: Responsive checkpoints already verified:
247: 
248: - `375x667`
249: - `390x844`
250: - `430x932`
251: - `768x1024`
252: - `1440x900`
253: 
254: For each viewport, the latest Task 8 audit confirmed:
255: 
256: - no vertical scroll
257: - no horizontal scroll
258: - board visible
259: - HUD visible
260: - controls visible
261: - overlay fits
262: - units tappable
263: - arrows readable
264: 
265: UI rules for future work:
266: 
267: - Do not solve layout by allowing page scroll.
268: - Do not add a footer, landing screen, or dashboard unless explicitly required.
269: - Do not add UI cards inside cards.
270: - Keep the shell compact and playable.
271: - If adding icons, prefer a real icon library only after dependency impact is justified.
272: - If adding assets, keep the SVG fallback path.
273: 
274: ## 5. Whole System State
275: 
276: Current production state:
277: 
278: - Git is initialized.
279: - The active branch is `stabilize-tribe-out`.
280: - Raw export, stabilization, cleanup, and Task 8 work have checkpoint commits.
281: - `PLAN.md` documents the workflow.
282: - `TASK.md` documents task completion and validation.
283: - `docs/audit/PREVIOUS_SCREEN_REUSE_AUDIT.md` documents previous-project reuse decisions.
284: - `scripts/task8-viewport-audit.mjs` verifies viewport behavior through Chrome DevTools Protocol.
285: - `codegraph` is initialized for fast code queries.
286: 
287: Current validation commands:
288: 
289: ```bash
290: npm run build
291: npm run typecheck
292: npm test
293: node scripts/task8-viewport-audit.mjs
294: ```
295: 
296: Current acceptance:
297: 
298: - Build passes.
299: - Typecheck passes.
300: - Unit tests pass.
301: - Viewport audit passes.
302: - Level 1 can be won.
303: - Replay works.
304: - Next level advances to level 2.
305: - Generated scaffold has been removed from runtime.
306: 
307: Current non-goals:
308: 
309: - No PixiJS.
310: - No audio.
311: - No raster asset integration.
312: - No backend.
313: - No auth.
314: - No leaderboard.
315: - No shop.
316: - No ads.
317: - No gacha or AFK systems.
318: 
319: Recommended future order:
320: 
321: 1. Add real assets only if files exist and map them through a central asset file.
322: 2. Add audio after the shell and gameplay remain stable.
323: 3. Add animation polish only after state transitions remain test-covered.
324: 4. Add new levels only with tests and solution notes.
325: 5. Consider PixiJS only if DOM rendering becomes a measured performance problem.
326: 
327: ## 6. Coins
328: 
329: Current coin behavior:
330: 
331: - Coins are a local reward counter.
332: - Each escaped unit adds coins.
333: - Winning a level adds bonus coins based on remaining lives.
334: - Coins persist in `localStorage`.
335: - Coins are loaded when the game starts.
336: - Coins are carried through restart and next-level flows.
337: 
338: Current coin purpose:
339: 
340: - Coins give the player a visible sense of progress.
341: - Coins reward efficient play because the win bonus includes remaining lives.
342: - Coins make level completion feel meaningful even without a shop or leaderboard.
343: 
344: Current coin effect:
345: 
346: - Coins currently do not unlock gameplay.
347: - Coins currently do not buy hints.
348: - Coins currently do not buy skins.
349: - Coins currently do not affect difficulty.
350: - Coins currently do not sync online.
351: 
352: Rules before expanding coins:
353: 
354: - Do not turn coins into a spendable economy until the economy is designed.
355: - Do not add a shop just because coins exist.
356: - Do not make hints cost coins until hint logic exists.
357: - Do not add paid upgrades, gacha, ads, or leaderboard coupling.
358: - If coins gain new effects, define the exact effect in docs first and add tests for the state transition.
359: 
360: Possible future coin uses:
361: 
362: - Cosmetic unlocks.
363: - Optional hint usage.
364: - Level-pack progress markers.
365: - Local achievement milestones.
366: 
367: These are not implemented yet.
